# Commit Workflow

When the user says **commit** (or asks to commit changes), always do these steps **in order**:

1. **Fix all errors and warnings** in the changed/related files (eslint, TypeScript/IDE diagnostics, obvious runtime issues). Do not leave known lint/build failures.
2. **Run Prettier** on the changed source files (or `npx prettier --write .` when appropriate).
3. **Commit** following the normal git safety protocol (status/diff/log, stage relevant files, HEREDOC message, verify status).
4. **Push** the branch to its remote (`git push` or `git push -u origin HEAD` if no upstream). Do not force-push unless the user explicitly asks.

**Never stage or commit Cursor rules** — keep `.cursor/` (including `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`) local only. It is gitignored; do not force-add it.

Do not skip prettier, lint cleanup, or push when the user only says “commit”.
